{
 "about": "Quaternius animals for Bandit Math. scale: model units to metres (the files are as made; makeAnimal scales them). height: metres at the withers (top of the shoulders); tall: top of the head standing idle; length: nose to tail. All face +Z. stride: how fast the clip carries it at clip speed 1 (m/s): how fast a foot that is down moves back under the body, the median over all four feet through the clip (rigs/animals/gait_measure.cjs), so a clip played at speed = pace / stride keeps its feet on the ground (the dogs' Walk barely plants its front feet: theirs is from the back feet). gait (the dogs): their own settings for gaitFor in src/actors/animals.js (their Walk is a slow amble; their Trot, made for the game, covers the paces between it and the Gallop). seat: where a saddle sits (offset in that bone's own space, model units; at: metres in the animal's own space, idle). lasso: the bone a rope loops round and the neck's radius there. Bone names are as three.js gives them (dots dropped: FrontShoulder.L is FrontShoulderL). The farm pack (farmCow, farmHorse, pig, sheep, pug; files in farm/) was exported from the pack's Cow/Horse/Pig/Pug/Sheep.blend files by the farm export rigs: clips Idle, Walk, WalkSlow, Gallop (the pack's Run, renamed so every animal answers to the same names), Jump and Death; the pig, sheep and pug had the horse's clips, so their strides were scaled down to their short legs and quickened (farm/fixes_<Name>.json there). The pug also has Trot, Sit_Down, Sit, Lie_Down and Lie (Lie is a sploot: back legs stretched out behind), made on its own rig by farm_dogclips.py. Their stride also lists WalkSlow (gaitFor doesn't use it); their bones: Body, Torso (the seat), Neck, Head (the rope goes round the neck just behind it), FrontFoot / BackFoot (the hooves and paws).",
